id=adb-hide-susfs
name=ADB Hide (susfs LKM x64)
version=v1.2.0
versionCode=5
author=ymuu (ADB subset ported from BRENE by rrr333nnn333)
description=Spoofs ADB runtime properties so apps read a clean state while real adbd stays usable. Uses resetprop only. v1.1 adds a live listener gate: init.svc.adbd is spoofed only when no TCP ADB endpoint is in LISTEN state, so wire protocol probes never contradict the spoof. REAL_DISABLE_ADB=1 in config.sh gives full BRENE parity. Watchdog re asserts spoofed props. v1.1.2 defers the USB config prop spoof until boot completed so Android no longer turns USB debugging off for real. v1.2.0: on an emulator, adbd listens on vsock only, so there is no TCP adb listener to probe and the init.svc.adbd spoof applies.
updateJson=
